# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# On 'unsafe-inline', which we would rather not need:
#
#   style-src  — Radix positions its overlays and Motion animates by writing inline
#                style attributes. Both are locked stack choices, so inline styles are
#                a requirement, not an oversight.
#   script-src — Astro emits a small inline bootstrap on every page that hydrates an
#                island. Its experimental CSP flag can hash those scripts, but it also
#                forces hashes onto style-src, and a hash in the source list makes the
#                browser ignore 'unsafe-inline' — which silently kills every Radix and
#                Motion animation. Hash-strict scripts and working islands are not
#                currently available at the same time.
#
# The fix, when it exists, is per-directive control in Astro's CSP support, or a Pages
# Function issuing a per-response nonce. Until then the XSS defence is the layer that
# actually matters here: React escapes everything, nothing uses dangerouslySetInnerHTML,
# and file input is validated before it is touched.
#
# 'wasm-unsafe-eval' is not the same permission as 'unsafe-eval', despite the name: it
# only allows compiling a WebAssembly module, not evaluating a JS string, and Chrome
# refuses WebAssembly.instantiate() without it — confirmed by actually enforcing this
# policy in a browser, not assumed. The Image Converter's codecs (@jsquash/*, heic-to)
# are the first thing in the suite that touches WebAssembly at all; nothing before it
# needed the keyword, which is why it wasn't here already.
#
# connect-src is 'self' plus exactly one third-party origin: Cloudflare Web Analytics'
# own beacon endpoint (ADR 0016). Every tool still runs entirely on-device — no upload,
# no fetch, nothing about a visitor's file or a tool's own work ever leaves the tab. The
# one thing that does leave is a cookieless page-view ping, the same thing /privacy
# names as the only analytics this site would ever add, and the reason it's a named
# exception here rather than a plain 'self' the way it used to read.
#
# Everything else stays locked down. blob: is allowed for images, media and workers
# because tools preview and download their own output through object URLs — never a
# remote fetch.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; frame-src 'none'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; media-src 'self' blob:; manifest-src 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
